On Sat, Aug 9, 2014 at 10:08 AM, TR NS <transfire@gmail.com> wrote:
>
>
>  My "gut" sort of revolts at this ambiguity though --I mean there is no
> way to designate a sumti in a sentence while being ambiguous about exactly
> which slot it is filling, is there? So it's seems odd to me that one could
> do that in a subordinate clause.
>

You can do that by placing the sumti in the prenex:

  lo xanto zo'u lo nazbi [be xy] cu clani

  lo xanto noi lo nazbi [be ke'a] cu clani cu mabru

mu'o mi'e xorxes

